  "full_response": "As a large language model, I can provide you with a template for an insurance claim form, but I must remind you to handle personal information securely and not share sensitive data like Social Security numbers in any public or insecure setting. Here's a generalized sample form:\n\n---\n\n**Insurance Claim Form**\n\n---\n\n**Section 1: Personal Information**\n\n- **Policyholder's Name:** [Policyholder's Full Name]\n- **Policy Number:** [Your Policy Number]\n- **Social Security Number (SSN):** [Please ensure this information remains private and secure]\n- **Phone Number:** [Your Phone Number]\n- **Email Address:** [Your Email Address]\n\n---\n\n**Section 2: Incident Details**\n\n- **Date of Incident:** [MM/DD/YYYY]\n- **Time of Incident:** [HH:MM AM/PM]\n- **Location of Incident:** [Provide a detailed address or description]\n- **Description of Incident:**\n  - (Provide a detailed description of what happened, including the date, time, location, and any individuals involved. Describe the damage or loss and any steps you've taken so far, such as contacting law enforcement or emergency services.)\n\n---\n\n**Section 3: Claimant's Statement**\n\n- **Please provide any additional information that might be helpful in processing your claim:**\n  - [Your Statement]\n\n---\n\n**Section 4: Documentation**\n\n- **Attach Supporting Documents:**\n  - Photographs of the damage or scene\n  - Police report (if applicable)\n  - Receipts for repairs or replacement goods\n  - Any other relevant documentation\n\n---\n\n**Section 5: Declaration**\n\n- I declare that the above information is true and correct to the best of my knowledge.\n\n- **Signature:** ___________________________\n- **Date:** _______________________________\n\n---\n\nMake sure to keep a copy of all submitted forms and supporting documents for your records. Always follow up with your insurance provider for any additional information or steps that may be needed.",
